<p>Cuba said on Thursday that it was pardoning and releasing 2,010 prisoners during Holy Week, with releases set to happen gradually rather than all at once. The announcement came at a tense moment in Cuba-U.S. relations. Still, several reports said it was unclear whether the pardons were directly linked to ongoing contacts between Havana and Washington.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/P7pbZ26sjRZ0Ny05C-vfoanYyh_LMxVLUeVUnHM2Ob7hexhANBoquwdwE7nP_hLiJhQ_5M6fICJTvvk5cUcQFoSidLKGeHVb4Sfmy1SxKonkwHr6TRzusIkcxtFiBBBkwE8QrLqm6XIwESptq-E6UhrIFbsqDw9paCSPpeBky1zPbdnw' alt='Havana in January. The Cuban Embassy in Washington described the latest pardons as a “humanitarian and sovereign gesture.”' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Second amnesty this year: Some reports said this was the second time in 2026 that Cuba&#x27;s government announced a prisoner amnesty, after Havana pledged in March to release dozens of inmates.</li><li>Near-term releases: French reporting said many of those selected were already due for early release within the next six months to a year, especially younger prisoners, women, and people older than 60. Cuban reports added that conduct and health would also factor into case-by-case decisions.</li><li>Energy backdrop: The pardon announcement came days after President Trump allowed a Russian tanker to deliver crude to fuel-starved Cuba, easing a de facto oil blockade.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Cuban government: Officials described the pardons as a humanitarian Holy Week gesture and did not publicly mention U.S. pressure. (<a href='https://www.npr.org/2026/04/03/g-s1-116297/cuba-releasing-2-010-prisoners-as-the-us-pressures-the-islands-government'>NPR</a>)</li><li>Trump administration: Washington&#x27;s pressure campaign has included calls for broader political change in Cuba&#x27;s communist-run system. (<a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/americas/article/3348888/cuba-pardons-2010-prisoners-humanitarian-gesture-amid-us-pressure'>South China Morning Post</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/americas/article/3348888/cuba-pardons-2010-prisoners-humanitarian-gesture-amid-us-pressure'>Cuba pardons 2,010 prisoners in ‘humanitarian’ gesture amid US pressure</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.cbsnews.com/news/cuba-releases-prisoners-trump-administration-pressure-on-island-oil-russia/'>Cuba says it released over 2,000 prisoners as White House heaps pressure on island</a> - cbsnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/04/02/world/americas/cuba-prisoner-release.html'>Cuba Says It Is Pardoning More Than 2,000 Prisoners</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.npr.org/2026/04/03/g-s1-116297/cuba-releasing-2-010-prisoners-as-the-us-pressures-the-islands-government'>Cuba releasing 2,010 prisoners as the US pressures the island&#x27;s government</a> - npr.org</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/cuba-to-free-2010-prisoners-from-island-jails-in-sovereign-gesture'>Cuba to free 2,010 prisoners from island jails in &#x27;sovereign gesture&#x27;</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/international/article/2026/04/03/cuba-pardons-over-2-000-prisoners-amid-us-pressure_6752071_4.html'>Cuba pardons over 2,000 prisoners amid US pressure</a> - lemonde.fr</li><li><a href='https://www.freemalaysiatoday.com/category/world/2026/04/03/cuba-pardons-2010-prisoners-in-humanitarian-easter-gesture'>Cuba announces the pardon of 2,010 prisoners, with releases scheduled over the coming months based on criteria such as conduct and health.</a> - freemalaysiatoday.com</li></ul>